Model code:
There are four main model py files available that should be used to run the model and compare the model outputs. This can be done in jupyter notebook or any other similar coding platform:
The file references for these models are:
- Copula_Based_Model
- Driver_Based_Model
- Hybrid_Based_Model
- Comparison

Supporting files:
The code relies on other supporting py files that are used by all models:
- reserves
- market_risks
- reinsurance
- generate_cat_losses
- catastrophes
- analysis


Model output:
The model results outputs are saved in excel and the charts are in PNG format.
- Copula_Based_Model_Output
- Driver_Based_Model_Output
- Hybrid_Based_Model_Output
